libportage
------------------------------------------
LibPortage is a fast and portable library offering functionality for doing
package management in a Gentoo system. This includes ebuilds, binpkgs and
managing a portage-compatible configuration. The library will provide all the
functions one may need to write a drop-in replacement for Portage in C.

Runtime requirements:
  cygwin-3.6.12-1
  libarchive13-3.8.11-1
  libportage-devel-0.1_alpha0-1bl2
  libportage0-0.1_alpha0-1bl2
  pkg-config-3.0.11-1

Build requirements:
(besides corresponding -devel packages)
  autoconf-20260320-3
  automake-20261107-1
  binutils-2.47-1
  cygport-0.37.13-1
  gcc-core-14.4.0-1
  libarchive-devel-3.8.11-1
  libtool-2.6.2-1
  make-4.4.1-2

Canonical website:
  https://github.com/larsuhartmann/libportage

Canonical download:
  https://github.com/larsuhartmann/libportage/archive/v0.1_alpha0.tar.gz

-------------------------------------------

Build instructions:
  1. unpack libportage-0.1_alpha0-X-src.tar.xz
  2. if you use setup to install this src package,
     it will be unpacked under /usr/src automatically
        % cd /usr/src
        % cygport ./libportage-0.1_alpha0-X.cygport all

This will create:
  /usr/src/libportage-0.1_alpha0-X-src.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libportage-0.1_alpha0-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libportage0-0.1_alpha0-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libportage-devel-0.1_alpha0-X.tar.xz

-------------------------------------------

